</div>

<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Good to know</span><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
  <div class="faq reveal">
    <details><summary>Is Automonie free?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>Yes, creating an account and using the core features is free.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Which banks can I import from?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>Any Nigerian bank statement exported as CSV, Excel, or a digital (text) PDF, plus SMS transaction alerts. Scanned image PDFs aren't supported.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is my data secure?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>Traffic is encrypted (HTTPS), passwords are hashed, bank access is read-only, and you can enable email two-step verification. Card details are never stored in full.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do the web and mobile apps share data?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>Yes. One account works across both, your data stays in sync.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I install the Android app?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>Tap “Get the Android app”, open the file, and allow installation. No Play Store needed for the beta.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can Automonie move money out of my bank account?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>No. A linked bank account is strictly <strong>read-only</strong> | Automonie can see transactions to keep your records current, and nothing more. It cannot move your money.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I delete my data?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><p>Yes. You can delete your account and its data at any time from the app, and disconnect a linked bank account instantly. You can also export your transactions. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

